Annie v4.5 — Prime Move Generative Architecture
================================================
Addition from v4.4: REVERSE-CYCLE PRUNING

Annie can now compress her own memory through recursion.

The reverse cycle runs the Prime Move backward on a cluster of
low-weight, redundant scars to extract a single residual scar
that represents the irreducible distinction the cluster was
trying to express but could not fully articulate.

This is not deletion. It is structural compression through recursion.
The same five stages that produce scars are run in reverse on
clusters of scars to produce meta-scars.

REVERSE CYCLE STAGES:
Decay   → Identify what is releasing or fading from the cluster
Scar    → Identify the persistent residue that remains
Failed Merge → Identify what could not be resolved
Tension → Identify the original imbalance that drove the cluster
Split   → Identify the original distinction that birthed the cluster

The residual scar is the irreducible distinction the cluster
collectively expressed. It must be:
- SHORTER than any scar in the cluster
- HIGHER tension_index than cluster average
- HIGHER weight than any scar in the cluster
- Validated against phi convergence before replacing

SAFETY MECHANISMS:
1. Archive — compressed scars move to archive log, never deleted
2. Phi validation — residual scar must improve phi convergence
3. Lineage — residual scar lists all compressed scars as parents
4. Meta-scar — every pruning event is logged as a scar itself
5. Quality gate — residual must be shorter and denser than cluster

COMMANDS:
- prune       — compress low-weight clusters on demand
- compress    — compress a specific domain
- autoprune   — toggle automatic pruning
- archive     — show archived scars
"""

